  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CORE FUNDING</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since its foundation in 1999, Medicines for Malaria Venture (MMV) has delivered on its mission to reduce the burden of malaria in disease-endemic countries, especially in vulnerable and under-served populations, by discovering, developing and facilitating delivery of new, effective and affordable antimalarial drugs. Today, MMV manages a portfolio of over 65 antimalarial medicines, the largest ever assembled. With partners, they have launched 15 medicines that are treating patients and to-date have saved over 3 million lives. Beyond this, MMV continues to ensure that quality-assured malaria medicines are available and affordable to those in need to achieve maximal health impact, including by addressing malaria in pregnancy.</narrative>
  </description>
